<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO 1996 net profit up 26 pct.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO 1996 net profit up 26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 calendar year.</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Total net profit (billions)	 3.30   vs   2.62</p>
<p>    Attributable net (billions)	 3.12   vs   2.37</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)		9.26   vs   7.69</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		   4.20   vs   3.60</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected banking group ABN AMRO Holding NV to report a 1996 net profit of 3.27-3.32 billion guilders and net attributable profit of 3.00-3.13 billion guilders.  </p>
<p>    Total assets (billions)	   595.26   vs 546.50</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity (billions)  22.96   vs  20.25</p>
<p>    Group capital (billions)	   40.38   vs  33.48</p>
<p>    BIS ratio (pct)			10.89   vs  10.80</p>
<p>    -- of which tier one capital	7.21   vs   6.51</p>
<p>    Total revenue (billions)	   19.09   vs  16.21</p>
<p>    Total expenses (billions)	  14.30   vs  12.36</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit (billions)	   4.79   vs   3.84</p>
<p>    Tax (billions)			  1.35   vs   1.12</p>
<p>    Minority interests		  141.00   vs 101.00</p>
<p>    Preference share dividend	 187.00   vs 248.00</p>
<p>    Net interest revenue (billions)  11.53   vs  10.24</p>
<p>    - Interest revenue (billions)    38.58   vs  36.30</p>
<p>    - Interest expense (billions)    27.05   vs  26.06</p>
<p>    Net commission income (billions)  4.96   vs   4.18</p>
<p>    Result fin transactions (blns)    1.88   vs   1.20</p>
<p>    Other revenue			 471.00   vs 389.00</p>
<p>Breakdown of results from financial transactions</p>
<p>     - foreign exchange trading     705.00   vs 613.00</p>
<p>     - securities trading	     781.00   vs 441.00</p>
<p>     - derivatives			323.00   vs 226.00</p>
<p>     - other			     73.00 vs loss 82.00</p>
<p>Breakdown of other revenue</p>
<p>     - leasing			    279.00   vs 240.00</p>
<p>     - insurance			   95.00   vs  59.00</p>
<p>     - other				 97.00   vs  90.00</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit breakdown by region</p>
<p>    - Netherlands (billions)	    2.70   vs   2.26</p>
<p>    - Rest of Europe		    290.00   vs 167.00</p>
<p>    - North America		     1,046    vs 733.00</p>
<p>    - Central and South America     454.00   vs 411.00</p>
<p>- Middle East, Far East</p>
<p>	and Africa			  300.00   vs 269.00</p>
